<title>SOUTH AFRICA: AMLAC YEAR SHR LEAPS, NO DIVIDEND.</title>
<headline>AMLAC YEAR SHR LEAPS, NO DIVIDEND.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31,</p>
<p>1996 vs proforma yr ended December 1995</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)	 </p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     19.60	vs     9.70</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		    5.19	vs     2.06</p>
<p>    Tax			  1.89	vs     0.59</p>
<p>    Finance costs	    0.97	vs     0.84</p>
<p>    Turnover		  48.52	vs     44.82</p>
<p>Full name: Amlac Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said it traded for four months in 1995 so</p>
<p>the results for 1995 had been restated as if businesses that now</p>
<p>forms part of Amlac had been part of the group as at December</p>
<p>31, 1995.</p>
<p>A dividend was not declared as it is company policy to</p>
<p>conserve cash resources, the firm said. The firm, however, plans</p>
<p>to declare a dividend for the current financial year.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
